CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 36 transform through optional-returning lambda: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=(0|10)$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
A capturing lambda converts to std::function<std::optional<T>(T)> and
is invoked through a member (the instructiont::transform shape from
CBMC's own sources, round-129 dog-food).  The libstdc++ constraint
chain _Requires<_Callable<F>> evaluates __invoke_result<F&,
_ArgTypes...> with the enclosing partial specialization's pack, which
must be pre-bound during member-template deduction ([temp.mem]); the
class-tag derivation must survive the function-type argument's
parentheses.  EXIT 10 tolerated: the harness still reports a no-body
for std::function's internal _Function_handler manager (separate,
pre-existing gap).
